<title>UK: BP intervenes to buy Norway oil assets from Conoco.</title>
<headline>BP intervenes to buy Norway oil assets from Conoco.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum Co Plc said it had bought additional stakes in the Norwegian Ula and Gyda oilfields from U.S. Conoco.</p>
<p>BP exercised its statutary option to buy the assets after Conoco -- a unit of DuPont Co -- agreed in September their sale to U.S. Amoco Corp.</p>
<p>BP's equity will be increased by 10 percent to 67.7 percent in Ula and 9.375 percent to 36 percent in Gyda, a BP staff newsletter said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
